  "assumptions": [
    "Fictional modern training scenario; country assignments are game settings, not historical service-date claims.",
    "DCS metres: x north, y east; altitude is MSL unless a condition explicitly says AGL. Positions, routes, terrain clearance and mission balance require DCS checks.",
    "Explicit stores are checked against bundled pydcs station compatibility; AI weapon employment and mission completion are not flight-verified.",
    "Director cues are fictional subtitles. No audio, real radar detection, JTAC service or authenticated procedure is configured.",
    "No external scripts or assets are required. The mission remains open after an outcome so the player can return; automatic recovery is not authored.",
    "The FARP authors a linked departure pad only. No support vehicles, repair/rearm/refuel entitlement, guaranteed FARP service or terrain-cleared pad placement is claimed.",
    "Helicopter waypoints are 1500 metres MSL, not terrain-following or nap-of-the-earth guidance. Inspect terrain clearance, obstacles, hover weight and FARP starts in DCS.",
    "CAS is a task and objective setup, not an automatic FAC/JTAC, nine-line, target designation, laser code, aircraft data-link or authenticated radio service.",
    "Weapon stations are catalogue-checked; player sensor use, guidance and actual kill effectiveness remain unverified. The wingman is AI and is not guaranteed to prosecute every group.",
    "Ground routes are generic waypoints. Stationary artillery vehicles are targets; no scripted firing mission or guaranteed ground assault behavior is supplied.",
    "Protected Destination counts surviving convoy units. Protected-1 is separately mandatory; destruction of another truck alone does not immediately fail the mission.",
    "Moving transport groups use native On Road routing; assault groups use native Rank (line abreast) movement. Road availability, deployment room and AI decisions require native verification; formations are authored rather than automatically selected on enemy contact."
